(GOVERNMENT OF INDIA - MINISTRY OF ELECTRONICS AND INFORMATION TECHNOLOGY) Tj
T*
(OPERATIONAL GUIDELINES: MEITY SAMRIDH SCHEME \(SAMRIDH\) / MEITY STARTUP HUB \(MSH\)) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(1. Overview & Objective:) Tj
T*
(Scheme for Accelerating Startups for Scale-up through Mentorship, Funding,) Tj
T*
(and Market Access, matching accelerator investments up to Rs. 40 Lakh per) Tj
T*
(software tech startup.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(2. Eligibility Criteria:) Tj
T*
(1. Software product startup with a demonstrable proof of concept,) Tj
T*
(   commercial traction, and customer validations.) Tj
T*
(2. Must be DPIIT recognized and registered in India.) Tj
T*
(3. Selected through a partner accelerator empanelled under MeitY SAMRIDH.) Tj
T*
(4. Indian promoter holding must be greater than 51%.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(3. Financial Assistance and Subsidy:) Tj
T*
(1. Matched funding up to Rs. 40 Lakh per startup along with 6-month customized) Tj
T*
(   accelerator cohort, corporate pilot linkages, and global investor demo) Tj
T*
(   day.) Tj
T*
(3. Maximum financial assistance cap is Rs 40.0 Lakh per unit.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(4. Mandatory Documents Checklist:) Tj
T*
(1. DPIIT Recognition Certificate) Tj
T*
(2. Product metrics and active customer traction report) Tj
T*
(3. Certificate of Incorporation) Tj
T*
(4. Cap table and valuation agreement from partnering accelerator) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(5. Application Procedure:) Tj
T*
(1. Mode: Online via MeitY Startup Hub \(MSH\) Portal) Tj
T*
(2. Official Portal: https://msh.meity.gov.in/samridh) Tj
T*
